results go to `results/` and `figures/`; the sensitivity goes to `results/sensitivity_90pct/` and `figures/sensitivity_90pct/`. Key result files are `summary.json`, `voxel_statistics.tsv.gz` (with voxel indices and MNI coordinates), `max_t_null.tsv`, NIfTI group maps, participant ROI estimates, and rendered figures. See [`report/report.md`](report/report.md) for interpretation.\nEOF\ncat > analysis/README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Analysis entry point\n\nThe frozen protocol is in [\"'`protocol.md`](protocol.md). Run [`run_analysis.py`](run_analysis.py) using the command in the root README. The default is the 100% shared nonzero-coverage mask; set `NARPS_COVERAGE_MIN=0.9` for the documented broader-mask sensitivity analysis. Results and figures are written under the corresponding folders named in the root README.\nEOF\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
